# The group von Neumann algebra `N(G)` and its trace

This file isolates the *analytic* input of the area.  For a countable group `G`:

* `N(G)` is the group von Neumann algebra, i.e. the commutant of the right regular
  representation on `ℓ²(G)`; it contains the left regular representation `ρ` of `G`;
* it carries a normal faithful tracial positive linear functional `τ`, the vector state
  `τ(a) = ⟨a δ₁, δ₁⟩`, with `τ(ρ(g)) = δ_{g,1}`;
* `N(G)` is directly finite (a factor of type `II₁`);
* every `a ∈ N(G)` has a range projection, so `N(G)` is a Baer `*`-ring;
* the set of non-zero-divisors of `N(G)` is an Ore set (Berberian), and the Ore
  localisation `U(G) = N(G)[(N(G)∖{0})⁻¹]` is the algebra of operators affiliated to
  `N(G)`.

The construction of `N(G)` from `ℓ²(G)` and the verification of these properties is the
"analysis" part of the project; here we record the interface and derive the algebraic
consequences that the rest of the project uses.

**State of the verification.**  For the concrete model `N(G) = ρ(G)'` of a countable group
**every** field of `GroupVonNeumannAlgebra` is *proved*, so that
`Work.ORVonNeumann.Rep.countableGroupVonNeumann : GroupVonNeumannAlgebra G` has no
hypotheses (`Submission.Work.ORVonNeumann.Rep.CountableVonNeumannOre`).  The ingredients:

* the Hilbert basis `{δ_g}` of `ℓ²(G)`, Parseval's identity
  (`Work.ORVonNeumann.Rep.parseval`) and the expansion
  `x = ∑' g, ⟪δ_g, x⟫ • δ_g` (`Work.ORVonNeumann.Rep.tsum_expansion`);
* the trace `τ` as a linear functional, `τ 1 = 1`, `τ` is `*`-preserving, positive and
  faithful (`Work.ORVonNeumann.Rep.tau` and its API), and **tracial**:
  `Work.ORVonNeumann.Rep.tau_tracial`;
* the **Baer property**: the right annihilator of every element is generated by a projection
  (`Work.ORVonNeumann.Rep.exists_rightAnnihilatorProjection`, mirror form
  `...exists_leftAnnihilatorProjection`);
* **direct finiteness**: `a * b = 1 → b * a = 1`
  (`Work.ORVonNeumann.Rep.directly_finite`);
* the left regular representation as a unitary, injective homomorphism `G →* N(G)` —
  `Work.ORVonNeumann.Rep.leftRegularHom`;
* the trace on projections is a dimension function with values in `[0,1]`
  (`Work.ORVonNeumann.Rep.tau_projection*`);
* **the Ore condition at non-zero-divisors** (`Work.Rep.oreSet_nonZeroDivisors`, via the
  square-root factorisation `Work.Rep.Ore.exists_sqrt_factorization`): in the finite Baer
  `*`-ring `N(G)` the non-zero-divisors form an Ore set (Berberian; Lück, *L²-Invariants*,
  Theorem 8.22).

## The concrete model and the division of labour

The concrete carriers are built in the sibling modules `Submission.Work.ORVonNeumann.Rep*`:
`ℓ²(G)` is `MeasureTheory.Lp ℂ 2 (Measure.count : Measure G)`, the right and left regular
representations are constructed there as unitary monoid homomorphisms into `B(ℓ²(G))`, the
group von Neumann algebra `Work.ORVonNeumann.groupVonNeumann G` is defined as the commutant
of the right regular representation, and `δ₁` is shown to be separating for it
(`Work.ORVonNeumann.Rep.delta1_separating`), with the vector state
`Work.ORVonNeumann.Rep.trace_vectorState`.

Everything is proved for `U(G)` too — `*`-regularity
(`Work.ORVonNeumann.VonNeumannAlgebra.starRegularAffiliated`), positive definiteness
(`...posDefAffiliated`), the faithful rank function (`...rankAffiliated`), and `ℂ[G] ↪ U(G)`
as a `*`-subalgebra (`...U`, `...UStar`) — with one exception, the subgroup data of
`StarRegularEnvelope`:

* the inclusions `U(H) ⊆ U(G)` for `H ≤ G` with Linnell independence (the last remaining
  field of `StarRegularEnvelope`; for infinite `G` only `H = ⊤` and `H = ⊥` are elementary).
  What *is* available here: `U(G)` is a `*`-ring containing `ℂ[G]` as a `*`-subalgebra
  (`Work.ORVonNeumann.VonNeumannAlgebra.U`, `...UStar`, with the involution
  `Work.ORVonNeumann.Ore.star_oreLocalization`).

All of these are recorded as fields of `GroupVonNeumannAlgebra` (and of
`StarRegularEnvelope`), each matched to its place in the literature.

For **finite** groups every one of these fields is proved and the instance is constructed in
`Submission.Work.ORVonNeumann.FiniteGroup`: `finiteGroupVonNeumann : GroupVonNeumannAlgebra G`
and `finiteGroupEnvelope : StarRegularEnvelope G`, with `U(G) = ℂ[G]` (a finite-dimensional
algebra, so all non-zero-divisors are units and the Ore localisation is trivial) and
`τ f = f.1` the canonical trace.  See `FiniteGroup/Examples.lean` for a concrete nontrivial
group.
-/
import Mathlib
import Submission.Work.ORVonNeumann.Basic
import Submission.Work.ORVonNeumann.SylvesterRank
import Submission.Work.ORVonNeumann.GroupAlgebraStar

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

namespace Work.ORVonNeumann

/-- A model of the group von Neumann algebra of `G`: the algebra `N` with its involution,
the left regular representation `ρ` (a `*`-monoid homomorphism into the unitaries), the
normal faithful trace `τ`, direct finiteness, the Baer `*`-ring property (range
projections) and the Ore condition at non-zero-divisors. -/
structure GroupVonNeumannAlgebra (G : Type u) [Group G] where
  /-- the von Neumann algebra `N(G)` -/
  N : Type u
  [ringN : Ring N]
  [starN : StarRing N]
  [algebraN : Algebra ℂ N]
  /-- the left regular representation -/
  ρ : G →* N
  ρ_star : ∀ g : G, star (ρ g) = ρ (g⁻¹)
  ρ_injective : Function.Injective ρ
  /-- the normal faithful trace `a ↦ ⟨a δ₁, δ₁⟩` -/
  τ : N →ₗ[ℂ] ℂ
  τ_one : τ 1 = 1
  τ_tracial : ∀ a b : N, τ (a * b) = τ (b * a)
  τ_star : ∀ a : N, star (τ a) = τ (star a)
  /-- `N(G)` is a `*`-algebra over `ℂ`: the involution is conjugate-linear in the scalars.
  (`StarModule ℂ N`; not a Mathlib instance because the axioms here are explicit.) -/
  star_smul : ∀ (c : ℂ) (x : N), star (c • x) = star c • star x
  τ_ρ_one : τ (ρ 1) = 1
  τ_ρ_ne_one : ∀ g : G, g ≠ 1 → τ (ρ g) = 0
  τ_re_nonneg : ∀ a : N, 0 ≤ (τ (star a * a)).re
  τ_faithful : ∀ a : N, τ (star a * a) = 0 → a = 0
  /-- `N(G)` is directly finite -/
  directly_finite : ∀ a b : N, a * b = 1 → b * a = 1
  /-- every element of `N(G)` has a range projection -/
  baer : ∀ a : N, ∃ p : N, IsStarProjection p ∧ ∀ x : N, a * x = 0 ↔ ∃ y : N, x = p * y
  /-- the Ore condition at non-zero-divisors (Berberian) -/
  oreSet : OreLocalization.OreSet (nonZeroDivisors N)

attribute [instance] GroupVonNeumannAlgebra.ringN GroupVonNeumannAlgebra.starN
  GroupVonNeumannAlgebra.algebraN GroupVonNeumannAlgebra.oreSet

namespace GroupVonNeumannAlgebra

variable {G : Type u} [Group G] (D : GroupVonNeumannAlgebra G)

/-- The trace of a self-adjoint square is real. -/
theorem tau_star_mul_self_im (a : D.N) : (D.τ (star a * a)).im = 0 := by
  have h1 : star (D.τ (star a * a)) = D.τ (star (star a * a)) := D.τ_star _
  rw [star_mul, star_star] at h1
  have h2 : star (D.τ (star a * a)) = D.τ (star a * a) := by
    rw [h1, D.τ_tracial]
  exact Complex.conj_eq_iff_im.mp h2

/-- The trace of a positive element is non-negative. -/
theorem tau_star_mul_self_re_nonneg (a : D.N) : 0 ≤ (D.τ (star a * a)).re :=
  D.τ_re_nonneg a

/-- The trace is faithful: `τ (a⋆ a) = 0` iff `a = 0`. -/
theorem tau_star_mul_self_eq_zero_iff (a : D.N) : D.τ (star a * a) = 0 ↔ a = 0 := by
  refine ⟨D.τ_faithful a, fun h => by simp [h]⟩

/-- `N(G)` is nontrivial, because `τ 1 = 1`. -/
theorem nontrivial : Nontrivial D.N := by
  refine ⟨0, 1, fun h => ?_⟩
  have h1 : D.τ (1 : D.N) = D.τ 0 := by rw [h]
  rw [D.τ_one, map_zero] at h1
  exact one_ne_zero h1

instance : Nontrivial D.N := D.nontrivial

/-- The image of a group element in `N(G)` is a unitary, in particular a unit. -/
theorem isUnit_ρ (g : G) : IsUnit (D.ρ g) := by
  refine ⟨⟨D.ρ g, D.ρ g⁻¹, ?_, ?_⟩, rfl⟩
  · rw [← map_mul, mul_inv_cancel, map_one]
  · rw [← map_mul, inv_mul_cancel, map_one]

theorem rho_star_mul (g : G) : star (D.ρ g) * D.ρ g = 1 := by
  rw [D.ρ_star, ← map_mul, inv_mul_cancel, map_one]

theorem rho_mul_star (g : G) : D.ρ g * star (D.ρ g) = 1 := by
  rw [D.ρ_star, ← map_mul, mul_inv_cancel, map_one]

/-- The linear extension of the regular representation to the group algebra `ℂ[G]`, i.e.
the inclusion `ℂ[G] ↪ N(G)`. -/
noncomputable def lift (f : MonoidAlgebra ℂ G) : D.N :=
  f.coeff.sum fun g c => c • D.ρ g

theorem lift_zero : D.lift (0 : MonoidAlgebra ℂ G) = 0 := by
  simp [lift]

theorem lift_single (g : G) (c : ℂ) :
    D.lift (MonoidAlgebra.single g c) = c • D.ρ g := by
  simp [lift, MonoidAlgebra.coeff_single]

theorem lift_one : D.lift (1 : MonoidAlgebra ℂ G) = 1 := by
  have h : (1 : MonoidAlgebra ℂ G) = MonoidAlgebra.single 1 1 := MonoidAlgebra.one_def.symm
  rw [h, lift_single, one_smul, map_one]

end GroupVonNeumannAlgebra

namespace GroupVonNeumannAlgebra

variable {G : Type u} [Group G]

/-- `U(G)`, the algebra of operators affiliated to `N(G)`: the Ore localisation of `N(G)`
at its set of non-zero-divisors (Berberian).  It is a `*`-regular positive definite ring
containing `ℂ[G]`, and it carries the extended rank function `rk_G`; these properties are
packaged in `StarRegularEnvelope`. -/
noncomputable abbrev affiliated (D : GroupVonNeumannAlgebra G) : Type u :=
  OreLocalization (nonZeroDivisors D.N) D.N

instance (D : GroupVonNeumannAlgebra G) : Ring D.affiliated :=
  inferInstanceAs (Ring (OreLocalization (nonZeroDivisors D.N) D.N))

instance (D : GroupVonNeumannAlgebra G) : Nontrivial D.affiliated :=
  inferInstanceAs (Nontrivial (OreLocalization (nonZeroDivisors D.N) D.N))

instance (D : GroupVonNeumannAlgebra G) : Algebra ℂ D.affiliated :=
  inferInstanceAs (Algebra ℂ (OreLocalization (nonZeroDivisors D.N) D.N))

end GroupVonNeumannAlgebra

end Work.ORVonNeumann
